IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-offence`
IMPORT `ccc7-s184-applications`
IMPORT `ccc7-s186-authorizations`

-- ccc7-tests-s186-authorizations.l4 -- tests for ccc7-s186-authorizations.l4 (ss 186, 186.1, 188, 188.1, 188.2). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

GIVEN statute IS A `s 183 statute`
      n IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 183 provision of an Act`
`s 186 test provision` MEANS `s 183 provision of an Act` WITH `statute` IS statute, `section` IS n, `subsection` IS sub

§ `Tests -- section 186(1.1) and section 186.1: the offences the two lists name (the same four limbs)`

-- 186(1.1) args: the judge is satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence, the offence, benefit of a group, criminal organization (s 2), terrorism offence (s 2)
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.111 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` 20.2 "(1)") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "where the judge is satisfied that": not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` FALSE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the four limbs
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: the group's status and the terrorism offence are for other sections
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` TRUE (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 186.1 args: the offence, benefit of a group, criminal organization (s 2), terrorism offence (s 2): "where the authorization is in relation to"
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.11 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.12 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52.2 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` 20.4 "(1)") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "where" fails: a "may ... where" grant is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (F11)
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.14 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 186 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- each period not exceeding one year (args: the day it begins, the day it ends, the answer for the offence)
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 28 2 2026) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the year of a leap day: 1 March 2023 to 29 February 2024 is one year; to 1 March 2024 is more
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 29 2 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 28 2 2026) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 186(1) and (2)`

-- (1) args: (a) best interests, (b) tried and failed, unlikely to succeed, urgency impractical, answer for (1.1)
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph (b) waived by (1.1)
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a failed "if" gate on a "may be given" grant is NOT COVERED (ruling of 2026-11-12)
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) args: the person is a solicitor (s 183), the place is a solicitor's office, residence or consultation place, the judge is satisfied of reasonable grounds
#ASSERT `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the judge ... is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor ... has been or is about to become a party to an offence"
#ASSERT `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not such a place: the bar does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) the duty: bound where the authorization concerns a place described in (2) (JUST FALSE where the "Where" fails), and whether kept
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge is bound to include terms and conditions to protect privileged communications` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge is bound to include terms and conditions to protect privileged communications` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge has included the terms and conditions` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge has included the terms and conditions` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge has included the terms and conditions` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 186(3) the judge has included the terms and conditions` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 186(4) to (8)`

-- (4)(e) args: the day the period begins, the day it ends, the answer for s 186.1
#ASSERT `s 186(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 29 4 2025) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 4 2025) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 186(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 4 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 186(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 4 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
